Practical 1: FTK IMAGE
1. Download and install FTK Imager from the official Exterro website.
2.Open The FTK
3. Go to File → Create Disk Image.
4. Select the Logical Drive
5. Select the Drive path next Choose the specific source drive from the list and click Finish.
6. Click Add
7.choose RAW (dd).
8. Enter case details.
8. Choose a destination folder and Finish
9.Ensure Verify images after they are created is checked
10. Open FTK Imager.
11. Go to File → Image Mounting.
12. Click Browse and select the forensic image file.
13. Choose the Mount Type Logical.
14. Click Mount.
15. Browse the mounted drive to view its files and folders as read-only evidence.
16. When finished, return to Image Mounting and click Unmount to safely detach the image

Practical 2: Checking the File System of a Drive[NTFS or FAT32]
Method 1: Using File Explorer
1. Open This PC in Disk management.
2. Right-click on Local Disk (C:) (or the drive to be checked).
3. Select Properties.
4. On the General tab, look at the File system field to see the format in use (for example, NTFS).
Practical 2.1: Viewing NTFS MACB Timestamps
1. Open Command Prompt
2. dir /T:C [Creation]
3. dir /T:W [Written]
4. dir /T:A [Accessed]
Practical 2.2: Viewing the NTFS USN Journal
1. Open Command Prompt as Administrator.
2. fsutil usn queryjournal C:
3. fsutil usn readjournal C:

